# Touch calibration for the bench kiosk, SHIPPED DISABLED ON PURPOSE.
#
# Read this before uncommenting anything.
#
# WHY IT IS DISABLED
#
# The rotation for this panel is set once, at the lowest layer, on the
# kernel command line:
#
#     video=DSI-1:800x480@60,panel_orientation=upside_down
#
# wlroots and weston both read the DRM panel orientation property and
# rotate the output, and libinput maps touch coordinates to the rotated
# output. So on a correctly configured board THIS FILE SHOULD NOT BE
# NEEDED, and a calibration matrix applied on top of a rotation that
# already worked rotates the touch surface a second time. The symptom is
# touch that works perfectly, upside down, which is the hardest version
# of this bug to reason about because every individual layer looks right.
#
# Measure before correcting:
#
#     libinput debug-events --verbose
#
# Touch the TOP LEFT of the picture. If the coordinates are near 0,0 the
# mapping is already correct and nothing here should be enabled.
#
# WHY THE DEVICE NAME IS NOT FILLED IN
#
# It differs between kernel versions and driver bindings. The project
# specification says it may read FT5406 or raspberrypi-ts, and the only
# way to know is to look at the board:
#
#     libinput list-devices | grep -A2 -i 'touch\|ft5\|raspberrypi'
#     bench-gfx input
#
# A rule with the wrong ATTRS{name} matches nothing and changes nothing,
# silently, which reads as "calibration did not help" and sends you
# looking at the compositor.
#
# HOW TO ENABLE IT
#
# Copy this file to /etc/udev/rules.d/, put the real device name in, and
# uncomment exactly one matrix line. Then:
#
#     udevadm control --reload
#     udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=input
#     systemctl restart weston
#
# The matrix is libinput's, in the order
#     xx xy x0  yx yy y0
# applied to normalised coordinates.

# 180 degree flip. The usual correction when the picture was rotated and
# the touch was not.
#ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="event[0-9]*", ATTRS{name}=="*FT5406*", \
#    ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="-1 0 1 0 -1 1"

# The same, for the other name the driver may present.
#ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="event[0-9]*", ATTRS{name}=="*raspberrypi-ts*", \
#    ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="-1 0 1 0 -1 1"

# Identity, for putting things back without deleting the file.
#ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="event[0-9]*", ATTRS{name}=="*FT5406*", \
#    ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="1 0 0 0 1 0"
